yday life in Suyeong and is popular with residents."],["Suyeong Community Culture Plaza","sight",35.172,129.1084,"Mangmi-ro","09:00–21:00","","","","r","A neighborhood public space used for small exhibitions, community events, and outdoor gatherings. Primarily serves residents but is accessible to visitors."],["Suyeong Fortress Gate Site","sight",35.1684,129.1149,"Suyeongseong-ro","09:00–18:00","","","","r","Archaeological remains marking the original gate location of Suyeong-eupseong, with signage explaining its historical role during the Joseon period."],["Mangmi-dong Ceramic Street","sight",35.1708,129.1092,"Mangmi-dong","Varies by shop","","","","r","A small cluster of ceramic studios and craft shops known among visitors interested in local arts and handmade goods."],["Suyeong Dwaeji Gukbap","restaurant",35.163,129.1125,"17 Suyeong-ro 680beon-gil","24 hours","","","","r","A classic Busan-style pork and rice soup. This restaurant is in the Suyeong Gukbap alley and is known for its deep, flavorful broth."],["Choryang Milmyeon (Suyeong)","restaurant",35.1645,129.113,"11 Suyeong-ro 724beon-gil","10:00-21:00","","","","r","A branch of one of Busan's most famous 'milmyeon' (wheat noodle) restaurants. Offers refreshing cold noodles, both spicy (bibim) and non-spicy (mul)."]]}